  "notes": "USAGE:\nA versatile word used for any kind of worsening — health, weather, relationships, economic conditions, environmental situations, etc. Frequently appears in news reports.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {悪化|あっか}: neutral, factual worsening\n- {深刻化|しんこくか}: becoming serious/grave (emphasizes severity)\n- {劣化|れっか}: degradation (often for materials or quality)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {症状|しょうじょう}が{悪化|あっか}する: symptoms worsen\n- {関係|かんけい}が{悪化|あっか}する: relations deteriorate\n- {治安|ちあん}の{悪化|あっか}: worsening public safety\n- {経済|けいざい}の{悪化|あっか}: economic deterioration\n- {悪化|あっか}の{一途|いっと}をたどる: to go from bad to worse",
